 "text": {
  "asOf": "2026-11-08",
  "fixed": [
   "Tideline asks whether NEAR Intents fees could ever cover the new NEAR being issued. This is research, not financial advice.",
   "A Bullish reading means the evidence passed a line set in advance, not that the price will rise."
  ],
  "live": [
   "As of 8 Nov, the verdict is held at Undecided because flow went private. The score is +3 of 7, but data lost to private flow may not move the verdict, so it stays Undecided until the treasury share falls back to 50% or less.",
   "Pointing Bullish: NEAR's share of fees is 34% over the last 30 days and revenue has risen over each of the last three months. In between: one integrator brings much of the fees but stays under the 80% line (SwapKit 75% of visible app fees). The DefiLlama figures come from a dataset nobody can re-run for free.",
   "Not measured because flow went private: Solver Competition (treasury 79% of USD). On the public swaps left, as side figures that set no reading: top 3 solvers hold 56%. Pricing Power is not settled: the data cannot yet say whether raising a fee helps or hurts revenue.",
   "The Confidential Intents treasury, where funds move to a private chain and the swap settles out of public view, carried 79% of the USD counted over the last 7 frozen days and 25% over the last 30. Other accounts' funds going into it were 85% of the flow we can see over 7 of the last 7 days, a side measure that sets no reading.",
   "A fall in these public numbers is not a fall in demand: swaps moving to the private chain leave the public record whether or not anyone stopped using them. What cannot be seen: fees on confidential swaps, which solver filled them, and any flow that stays shielded.",
   "Monthly volume would need to reach about 3.3x today's level under the 1.6% issuance plan, which passed its vote but is not in force yet, or 5.1x if issuance stays at 2.5%, with all revenue spent on buybacks."
  ]
 }
